\title{Topological ordering means "edges all point to the right"}
\date{2026-09-24T15:43:34Z}
\tag{algorithms}
\taxon{Remark}
\tag{draft}

\import{algorithms-macros}

\p{In other words, a [topological ordering](00NB) is a way to put the vertices of a graph in order so that the edges only point to the right.  This corresponds to a consistent order in which classes can be taken, tasks can be done, \em{etc.} so the prerequisites are always met.}

